; The target-independent AST containers (.ai/asm_plan.md §4).
;
; Note what is *not* here. Two things, for two different reasons:
;
; - the TARGET signature. This package must not depend on target_intf, because
;   §5.1's dependency direction runs the other way - a target description
;   depends on the generic machinery and never the reverse. The ASTs are
;   parameterized over the target's instruction types rather than functorized
;   over TARGET, which is what makes that possible: a container holding an
;   'insn needs no interface to hold it.
;
; - the front end. Lexer, grammar, token slices and the source AST moved to
;   asm_syntax, so that everything downstream of a parsed line can be linked
;   without them. What is left is what an assembled instruction is made of:
;   expressions, section permissions, directives, and the staged ASTs.

(library
 (name asm_core)
 (modes byte native)
 (libraries foundation fmt)
 (enabled_if
  (<> %{env:ASM_MELANGE=false} true)))
